-- title:
--   Equality of two morphisms over a finitely generated ideal
-- statement:
--   Let $S$ be a commutative ring and let $X,Y$ be schemes (in universe $0$). Let $f : X \to \operatorname{Spec} S$ be proper, flat and locally of finite presentation, and let $g : Y \to \operatorname{Spec} S$ be separated, flat and locally of finite presentation. Assume given a sheaf of modules $\mathcal L_X$ on $X$ which is invertible, in the sense that every point of $X$ has an open neighbourhood $U$ such that the pullback of $\mathcal L_X$ along $U \hookrightarrow X$ is isomorphic to the unit module over the structure sheaf of $U$, and which satisfies `ClosedImmersionBySections` for $f$: for some $N$ there are global sections $\sigma_0,\dots,\sigma_N$ of $\mathcal L_X$ together with a morphism $X \to \operatorname{Proj}$ of the graded ring of polynomials in $N+1$ variables over $S$ which composed with the projection to $\operatorname{Spec} S$ is $f$, such that over the preimage of each basic open set $D(X_i)$ multiplication by the restriction of $\sigma_i$ is bijective on sections and the pulled-back ratio $X_j/X_i$ carries $\sigma_i$ to $\sigma_j$, and such that this morphism to $\operatorname{Proj}$ is a closed immersion; assume the same data $\mathcal L_Y$ for $g$. Let $u,v : X \to Y$ satisfy $g \circ u = f$ and $g \circ v = f$. Then there is a finitely generated ideal $J \subseteq S$ such that for every commutative ring $T$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi : S \to T$, the two composites of the first projection $X \times_{\operatorname{Spec} S} \operatorname{Spec} T \to X$ with $u$ and with $v$ are equal if and only if the ideal of $T$ generated by $\varphi(J)$ is zero.
--
--   This is the statement that the locus in the base where two $S$-morphisms of a proper flat family coincide is a closed subscheme of $\operatorname{Spec} S$ cut out by a finitely generated ideal — the ideal-theoretic form of Grothendieck's scheme of coincidences attached to the Hom-scheme. It is used in the construction of the closed locus where a framed polarised abelian scheme satisfies a translation condition, via [`AlgebraicGeometry.FramedPolarisedAbelianScheme.exists_ideal_fg_forall_isPullback_translate_comp_eq_iff_map_eq_bot_of_section`](thm.html#AlgebraicGeometry.FramedPolarisedAbelianScheme.exists_ideal_fg_forall_isPullback_translate_comp_eq_iff_map_eq_bot_of_section).
